[{:db/id 17592186171953 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5e37b600-123f-57a8-aec0-1c4187d7acd1" "question-e43445a0-0d82-5a10-9128-a6bbc70f2fb7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171739 :question/problem "Evaluate $31^2.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate $31^2,$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n![](images/0f/0f6a4e089111de1dbb0e16cb6c388d3dcd236e981f94e2b4694c3492e3d526a3.svg)\n\nThen, we work out $31 \\times 31.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $31 \\times 31 =   961.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171954 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-25c765b2-1047-5099-8c3e-89ccf0cb03b6" "question-c6078b88-7674-57bc-95ac-a34e18c2f27b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171759 :question/problem "Evaluate $220^2.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate $220^2,$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n![](images/e9/e963c6c194b0cf3991be02d43f130eb81cd3e6f16b1b6921718468b3752ddc07.svg)\n\nThen, we work out $220 \\times 220.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}220 & \\,⟶\\,220 \\\\ 220 & \\,⟶\\,220\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $2$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}484}{\\color{blue}00}= 48,400\n$$\n\nTherefore, $220^2  =   48,400.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171955 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f2152ba3-455d-5581-bc1a-a5346e3a471a" "question-bbc9b46d-06dd-559d-bf07-a16e533c79e9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171738 :question/problem "Evaluate $7^4.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the definition, \n![](images/90/90f05ddf350a2b7a739a219c2dbb35958fd182ee9e665e0e5f6ce317ba7675ed.svg)\n\nSince $7 \\times 7 = 49,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{7 \\times 7}_{\\color{blue}49} \\times \\underbrace{7 \\times 7}_{\\color{blue}49} = {\\color{blue}49} \\times {\\color{blue}49}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $49 \\times 49.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\color{blue}3[/math]}} \\\\ \\boxed{\\text{[math]\\color{blue}8[/math]}}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7^4=2,401.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5e37b600-123f-57a8-aec0-1c4187d7acd1" :question/id #uuid "5e37b600-123f-57a8-aec0-1c4187d7acd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103854" :question/problem "${21}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate ${21}^{2},$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n\n$$\n{21}^{2}={{21\\times 21}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out $21\\times 21.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${21}^{2}=441.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c341d955-1902-5827-913d-e306ac904cea"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c341d955-1902-5827-913d-e306ac904cea" :answer-field/id #uuid "c341d955-1902-5827-913d-e306ac904cea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-84507046-5d4e-53b2-b7bf-b7a74f9e31f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a57f602c-e405-5d4c-b0ed-356fbf84d770" "answer-9686d914-1ae2-54bb-a298-e30f4ea05fb1" "answer-7814b84e-31e9-5b25-b1d2-682afc124ca3" "answer-cfccb0b0-2e66-5b26-9cb9-c8a973494329