,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${14}^{2}=196.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6ced82ff-6330-5b2d-9d1d-4a8a84518b30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6ced82ff-6330-5b2d-9d1d-4a8a84518b30" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ced82ff-6330-5b2d-9d1d-4a8a84518b30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d2180c52-0c69-5616-9e0e-538f8bf11655" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2180c52-0c69-5616-9e0e-538f8bf11655"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2180c52-0c69-5616-9e0e-538f8bf11655" :answer/id #uuid "d2180c52-0c69-5616-9e0e-538f8bf11655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "196" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-25c765b2-1047-5099-8c3e-89ccf0cb03b6" :question/id #uuid "25c765b2-1047-5099-8c3e-89ccf0cb03b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-224272" :question/problem "${160}^{2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate ${160}^{2},$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n\n$$\n{160}^{2}={{160\\times 160}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out $160\\times 160.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}160 & \\,⟶\\,160 \\\\ 160 & \\,⟶\\,160\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $2$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{3}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n25600=25,600\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${160}^{2}=25,600.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1f42ed49-0e4f-50d7-b2dc-b6a989999e04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1f42ed49-0e4f-50d7-b2dc-b6a989999e04" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f42ed49-0e4f-50d7-b2dc-b6a989999e04" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6181b2f4-70eb-592e-8e28-5dbb8add845c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6181b2f4-70eb-592e-8e28-5dbb8add845c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6181b2f4-70eb-592e-8e28-5dbb8add845c" :answer/id #uuid "6181b2f4-70eb-592e-8e28-5dbb8add845c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25600" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c6078b88-7674-57bc-95ac-a34e18c2f27b" :question/id #uuid "c6078b88-7674-57bc-95ac-a34e18c2f27b" :question/math-academy-id "q-224264" :question/problem "${700}^{2}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate ${700}^{2},$ we start by writing it out with a multiplication sign:\n\n$$\n{700}^{2}={{700\\times 700}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nThen, we work out $700\\times 700.$\n\nFirst, we figure out the non-zero part and the block of zeros for both numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}700 & \\,⟶\\,700 \\\\ 700 & \\,⟶\\,700\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that there are $4$ zeros in total.\n\nNext, we multiply the non-zero parts:\n\n$$\n7\\times 7=49\n$$\n\nFinally, we join the above with the block of zeros: \n\n$$\n490000=490,000\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${700}^{2}=490,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3854e34a-bad6-5250-b016-0e9032322e89"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3854e34a-bad6-5250-b016-0e9032322e89" :answer-field/id #uuid "3854e34a-bad6-5250-b016-0e9032322e89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5e22584d-3050-5603-88da-5ecc5679e6e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e22584d-3050-5603-88da-5ecc5679e6e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e22584d-3050-5603-88da-5ecc5679e6e1" :answer/id #uuid "5e22584d-3050-5603-88da-5ecc5679e6e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "490000" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f2152ba3-455d-5581-bc1a-a5346e3a471a" :question/id #uuid "f2152ba3-455d-5581-bc1a-a5346e3a471a" :question/math-academy-id "q-224334" :question/problem "Given that ${26}^{2}=676,$ evaluate ${26}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate ${26}^{4},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{26}^{4}={{26\\times 26\\times 26\\times 26}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nSince ${26}^{2}=26\\times 26=676,$ we have\n\n$$\n{{26\\times 26}_{⏟}}_{676}\\times {{26\\times 26}_{⏟}}_{676}=676\\times 676.\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $676\\times 676.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ \\cancel{5} \\\\ \\cancel{4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ \\cancel{4} \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${26}^{2}=456,976.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73ad5707-2679-50c7-b949-eced3d654331"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73ad5707-2679-50c7-b949-eced3d654331" :answer-field/id #uuid "73ad5707-2679-50c7-b949-eced3d654331" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1a1fe2e9-3215-56ff-844d-809607dfee80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2f293bda-663a-5011-a208-7a934bda6945" "answer-cc334405-0655-5d39-b908-539af151fd5c" "answer-1a1fe2e9-3215-56ff-844d-809607dfee80" "answer-d47068e5-5d78-5c8f-913c-edd528905913" "answer-210645d8-4956-5453-83b8-3f0cd0d18de8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f293bda-663a-5011-a208-7a934bda6945" :answer/id #uuid "2f293bda-663a-5011-a208-7a934bda6945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "262,626" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc334405-0655-5d39-b908-539af151fd5c" :answer/id #uuid "cc334405-0655-5d39-b908-539af151fd5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45,676" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a1fe2e9-3215-56ff-844d-809607dfee80" :answer/id #uuid "1a1fe2e9-3215-56ff-844d-809607dfee80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "456,976" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d47068e5-5d78-5c8f-913c-edd528905913" :answer/id #uuid "d47068e5-5d78-5c8f-913c-edd528905913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46,766" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-210645d8-4956-5453-83b8-3f0cd0d18de8" :answer/id #uuid "210645d8-4956-5453-83b8-3f0cd0d18de8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "546,796" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bbc9b46d-06dd-559d-bf07-a16e533c79e9" :question/id #uuid "bbc9b46d-06dd-559d-bf07-a16e533c79e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-224328" :question/problem "Given that ${15}^{2}=225,$ evaluate ${15}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate ${15}^{4},$ we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{15}^{4}={{15\\times 15\\times 15\\times 15}_{⏟}}_{4\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nSince ${15}^{2}=15\\times 15=225,$ we have\n\n$$\n{{15\\times 15}_{⏟}}_{225}\\times {{15\\times 15}_{⏟}}_{225}=225\\times 225.\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $225\\times 225.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\cancel{0} \\\\ \\cancel{1}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\cancel{1} \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${15}^{4}=50,625.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0d982c32-a336-5d10-8464-7705dd1cba12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d982c32-a336-5d10-8464-7705dd1cba12" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d982c32-a336-5d10-8464-7705dd1cba12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b3c3a767-02dd-5d0f-8568-320f3e0f1f36" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e16b1bed-cf77-5fd6-b458-9e563702d67f" "answer-cbca9429-182d-53fc-9991-dd37c193bd21" "answer-b3c3a767-02dd-5d0f-8568-320f3e0f1f36" "answer-89dbb185-61b3-5c47-890c-db13f2de2ed5" "answer-f746371d-17a0-5ecb-9e89-1503dc6e6ce6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e16b1bed-cf77-5fd6-b458-9e563702d67f" :answer/id #uuid "e16b1bed-cf77-5fd6-b458-9e563702d67f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25,025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbca9429-182d-53fc-9991-dd37c193bd21" :answer/id #uuid "cbca9429-182d-53fc-9991-dd37c193bd21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5,625" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3c3a767-02dd-5d0f-8568-320f3e0f1f36" :answer/id #uuid "b3c3a767-02dd-5d0f-8568-320f3e0f1f36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50,625" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89dbb185-61b3-5c47-890c-db13f2de2ed5" :answer/id #uuid "89dbb185-61b3-5c47-890c-db13f2de2ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6,525" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f746371d-17a0-5ecb-9e89-1503dc6e6ce6" :answer/id #uuid "f746371d-17a0-5ecb-9e89-1503dc6e6ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60,515" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186173277 :tutorial/content "To evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product. \n\nFor example, let's evaluate $2^4.$\n\nFirst, we write\n![](images/4c/4ccd929bbf46272fe64264465ed639c841643ec0e6c42d053d66555faa910dff.svg)\n\nSince $2 \\times 2 = 4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $4\\times 4.$\nSince $4\\times 4=16,$ we conclude that \n\n$$\n2^4=16.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172209 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
